{
  "info": {
    "name": "PRISM \u00b7 VocX voice capture (via NGINX)",
    "description": "The voice pipeline end to end, through the edge (/vocx/v1/*): capabilities \u2192 capture PREVIEW (extraction + confidence gate + write plan; never writes) \u2192 COMMIT (idempotent by capture_id: Register writes as svc_vox, the RM's Google Calendar when connected) \u2192 search the interaction log. Google connect is a browser flow: open {{baseUrl}}/vocx/v1/auth/start?rm=Priya&go=1 (the gateway exempts only the CALLBACK from require_auth). Works in BOTH postures: run request 00 first \u2014 with dexUrl set it signs in and every call carries the bearer; with dexUrl empty it skips and header trust applies.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "00 \u00b7 POST /dex/token \u2014 sign in (skips itself in the dev posture)",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/x-www-form-urlencoded"
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{dexUrl}}/dex/token",
          "host": [
            "{{dexUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "dex",
            "token"
          ]
        },
        "body": {
          "mode": "urlencoded",
          "urlencoded": [
            {
              "key": "grant_type",
              "value": "password"
            },
            {
              "key": "client_id",
              "value": "prism"
            },
            {
              "key": "scope",
              "value": "openid email profile"
            },
            {
              "key": "username",
              "value": "{{rmEmail}}"
            },
            {
              "key": "password",
              "value": "{{ssoPassword}}"
            }
          ]
        },
        "description": "Needed only in the PRODUCTION POSTURE (prod-posture overlay + --profile sso): REQUIRE_AUTH means identity comes ONLY from a verified bearer, and this captures the ID TOKEN as vocxToken for every following request. With dexUrl empty (dev posture) the request SKIPS ITSELF and the gateway trusts X-User-Email instead. Identities: e2e.rm@ / e2e.maker@ / e2e.checker@evamfinance.com, password 'prism' (deploy/compose/dex/config.yaml)."
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "prerequest",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "// Transport failures (Dex not running) never reach the test script,",
              "// so the dev-posture guard must live HERE or --bail would abort.",
              "if (!pm.environment.get('dexUrl')) {",
              "  pm.environment.set('vocxToken', '');",
              "  console.log('dexUrl empty \u2014 dev posture, header trust.');",
              "  if (pm.execution && pm.execution.skipRequest) pm.execution.skipRequest();",
              "}"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
              "  const b = pm.response.json();",
              "  pm.environment.set('vocxToken', b.id_token || '');",
              "  pm.test('signed in (id_token)', () => pm.expect(b.id_token).to.be.a('string'));",
              "} else {",
              "  pm.environment.set('vocxToken', '');",
              "  console.log('Dex sign-in failed \u2014 status ' + pm.response.code);",
              "  pm.test('Dex sign-in', () => pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.eql(200));",
              "}"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
